<title>USA: Consumers restarts 780 MW Mich. nuke - NRC.</title>
<headline>Consumers restarts 780 MW Mich. nuke - NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co restarted its 780 megawatt (MW) Palisades nuclear power plant following a refueling and maintenance outage that began in early November, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Friday.</p>
<p>In its daily plant status report, NRC said the South Haven, Michigan generating station was running at low power, about three percent of capacity, amid startup testing.</p>
<p>Consumers Power is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
